# The ruling: the delayed ability "will trigger any time you lose control of that Equipment this turn, whether it's because
# the 'until end of turn' duration ended or because someone else gained control of the Equipment with another effect".
# Bot1 takes Bot2's Skullclamp onto its Grizzly Bears, then gives the Skullclamp to Bot2 with Harmless Offering in the
# same main phase. Bot1 lost control (CR 613.1b) while the Skullclamp was attached to a creature Bot1 controls (CR
# 603.4), so it is unattached at once - the Bears are 2/2 again before the turn ends.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Grizzly Bears
Stolen Uniform
Black Lotus
Harmless Offering
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Skullclamp
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Skullclamp.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stolen Uniform.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Harmless Offering.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Skullclamp)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl; Grizzly Bears
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Power = 2
Bot1.Graveyard = Harmless Offering; Black Lotus; Stolen Uniform
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Skullclamp
Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = (absent)
